    question: 'Can I bring a power bank on a plane?',
    answer: '<p><strong>Yes, but with restrictions.</strong> TSA and airline rules:</p><ul><li><strong>Carry-on only:</strong> Power banks must be in your carry-on bag, never checked luggage</li><li><strong>Capacity limit:</strong> Under 100Wh (approximately 27,000mAh at 3.7V) without approval</li><li><strong>100-160Wh:</strong> Allowed with airline approval (most laptops)</li><li><strong>Over 160Wh:</strong> Generally prohibited</li><li><strong>Quantity:</strong> Most airlines allow 2 power banks per passenger</li></ul><p>Our top picks (Anker 737 at 86.4Wh, Zendure SuperTank at 96.48Wh) are within the 100Wh limit for hassle-free travel.</p>'
