    question: 'Is wireless charging worth it on a power bank?',
    answer: '<p><strong>Convenient but slower.</strong> Trade-offs:</p><p><strong>Pros:</strong></p><ul><li>No cable needed (one less thing to carry)</li><li>Magnetic (MagSafe) stays attached to phone</li><li>Convenient for quick top-ups</li></ul><p><strong>Cons:</strong></p><ul><li>Slower: 7.5-15W wireless vs 20-30W+ wired</li><li>Less efficient (energy lost as heat)</li><li>Adds cost and weight</li></ul><p>Our take: Wireless is great for iPhone users with MagSafe (Anker 622 MagGo). For fastest charging or Android, stick with wired USB-C PD.</p>'
  },
