---

<ArticleLayout
    title={title}
    description={description}
    author={author}
    authorUrl={authorUrl}
    pubDate={pubDate}
    readingTime={readingTime}
    image={image}
    imageAlt={imageAlt}
    category="Accessories"
    categorySlug="gear"
    headings={headings}
>
  <!-- Introduction -->
  <h2 id="introduction">Never Run Out of Power on the Road</h2>
  <p>
    For digital nomads, a dead battery means lost productivity—or worse, being stranded without communication.
    A quality portable charger is essential travel gear, right alongside your laptop and passport.
  </p>
  <p>
    We tested 10 portable chargers across four months of travel, evaluating capacity accuracy, charging speed,
    build quality, and real-world usefulness for digital nomads.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Quick answer:</strong> The <a href="#anker-737">Anker 737 PowerCore</a> is our top pick for digital
    nomads who need laptop charging—140W output handles even MacBook Pros at full speed. For phone-only users,
    the <a href="#anker-magsafe">Anker 622 MagGo</a> is perfect for iPhone with its magnetic wireless charging.
    On a budget, the <a href="#iniu-budget">INIU 10000mAh</a> delivers excellent value at just $20.
  </p>

  <!-- Quick Picks -->
  <h2 id="quick-picks">Our Top 3 Portable Charger Picks</h2>
  <p>Short on time? Here are our top recommendations:</p>
  <ComparisonTable
      columns={quickPicksColumns}
      rows={quickPicksRows}
      caption="Top 3 portable chargers for travel"
  />
  <p>
    Keep reading for detailed reviews of all 8 chargers we tested, plus guidance on TSA rules and laptop charging.
  </p>

  <!-- Understanding Capacity -->
  <h2 id="understanding-capacity">Understanding Power Bank Capacity</h2>
  <p>
    Power bank capacity is measured in mAh (milliamp-hours) or Wh (watt-hours). Here's what the numbers mean
    in practical terms:
  </p>

  <h3>Capacity Quick Guide</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>5,000mAh:</strong> 1 full phone charge, pocket-sized, emergency backup</li>
    <li><strong>10,000mAh:</strong> 2-3 phone charges, daily carry, light travel</li>
    <li><strong>20,000mAh:</strong> 4-5 phone charges or partial laptop charge, multi-day trips</li>
    <li><strong>25,000+mAh:</strong> Full laptop charges, maximum capacity for serious travel</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Real-World Expectations</h3>
  <p>
    Advertised capacity is always higher than usable capacity. Expect 65-85% efficiency due to:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Voltage conversion losses</li>
    <li>Heat dissipation</li>
    <li>Cable resistance</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    A 20,000mAh power bank realistically delivers about 13,000-17,000mAh to your devices.
  </p>

  <!-- Detailed Reviews -->
  <h2 id="detailed-reviews">Portable Charger Detailed Reviews</h2>

  <!-- Anker 737 PowerCore -->
  <h3 id="anker-737">1. Anker 737 PowerCore — Best for Laptop Charging</h3>
  <p>
    The Anker 737 is the most powerful portable charger we tested, capable of charging laptops at full speed
    with its 140W output. It's the go-to choice for digital nomads who need to keep laptops powered on the go.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What makes it stand out:</strong> 140W USB-C PD output charges even the 16" MacBook Pro at maximum
    speed. Smart digital display shows remaining capacity, estimated time, and output wattage. Build quality
    is exceptional.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Key specifications:</strong>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Capacity:</strong> 24,000mAh (86.4Wh)</li>
    <li><strong>Output:</strong> 140W USB-C, 18W USB-A × 2</li>
    <li><strong>Input:</strong> 140W USB-C (full recharge in 1.5 hours)</li>
    <li><strong>Ports:</strong> 2× USB-C, 1× USB-A</li>
    <li><strong>Weight:</strong> 1.3 lbs (632g)</li>
    <li><strong>Dimensions:</strong> 6.1" × 2.2" × 1.9"</li>
    <li><strong>Display:</strong> Smart digital display</li>
    <li><strong>TSA:</strong> Approved (under 100Wh)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Pros:</strong>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>140W output charges any laptop at full speed</li>
    <li>Smart display shows useful information</li>
    <li>Recharges itself in 1.5 hours</li>
    <li>Premium Anker build quality</li>
    <li>TSA-approved capacity</li>
    <li>24-month warranty</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Cons:</strong>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>$110 is expensive</li>
    <li>1.3 lbs is heavy for daily carry</li>
    <li>Too bulky for pants pockets</li>
    <li>Only one USB-A port</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Pricing:</strong> $110 (often on sale for $90-100)
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Best for:</strong> Digital nomads who work from cafes, airports, and need reliable laptop charging.
    The investment pays off in productivity gains.
  </p>
  <AffiliateButton
      href="/go/amazon/anker-737"
      text="Check Anker 737 Price on Amazon"
      variant="primary"
      program="amazon"
  />

  <!-- Anker 622 MagGo -->
  <h3 id="anker-magsafe">2. Anker 622 MagGo — Best for iPhone Users</h3>
  <p>
    The Anker 622 MagGo is a slim, magnetic wireless charger that attaches directly to iPhone 12 and newer.
    It's the most convenient way to keep your iPhone charged throughout the day.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What makes it stand out:</strong> MagSafe-compatible magnets snap onto your iPhone and stay
    attached. Built-in kickstand props up your phone for video calls. Slim enough to use while holding your
    phone.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Key specifications:</strong>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Capacity:</strong> 5,000mAh</li>
    <li><strong>Output:</strong> 7.5W wireless, 12W USB-C</li>
    <li><strong>Input:</strong> USB-C</li>
    <li><strong>Weight:</strong> 0.3 lbs (140g)</li>
    <li><strong>Dimensions:</strong> 4.1" × 2.6" × 0.5"</li>
    <li><strong>Compatibility:</strong> iPhone 12/13/14/15/16 (MagSafe)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Pros:</strong>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Magnetic attachment is super convenient</li>
    <li>Built-in kickstand for video calls</li>
    <li>Slim and lightweight</li>
    <li>No cable needed for charging</li>
    <li>Multiple colors available</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Cons:</strong>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>5,000mAh is only ~1 phone charge</li>
    <li>7.5W wireless is slower than wired</li>
    <li>iPhone only (MagSafe requirement)</li>
    <li>Adds bulk when attached</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Pricing:</strong> $50
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Best for:</strong> iPhone users who want convenient top-up charging without cables. Great for
    meetings, conferences, and daily carry.
  </p>
  <AffiliateButton
      href="/go/amazon/anker-622-magsafe"
      text="Check Anker 622 MagGo Price on Amazon"
      variant="primary"
      program="amazon"
  />

  <!-- Zendure SuperTank Pro -->
  <h3 id="zendure-supertank">3. Zendure SuperTank Pro — Maximum Capacity</h3>
  <p>
    The Zendure SuperTank Pro offers the most capacity you can fly with (barely under 100Wh) and includes an
    OLED display for detailed status information. It's built like a tank and charges like one too.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Key specifications:</strong>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Capacity:</strong> 26,800mAh (96.48Wh)</li>
    <li><strong>Output:</strong> 100W USB-C × 2, 15W USB-A × 2</li>
    <li><strong>Input:</strong> 100W USB-C (full recharge in 2 hours)</li>
    <li><strong>Ports:</strong> 2× USB-C, 2× USB-A</li>
    <li><strong>Weight:</strong> 1.4 lbs (650g)</li>
    <li><strong>Display:</strong> OLED with detailed info</li>
    <li><strong>TSA:</strong> Approved (under 100Wh)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Pros:</strong>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Maximum flight-legal capacity</li>
    <li>100W charges most laptops</li>
    <li>4 ports for multiple devices</li>
    <li>Detailed OLED display</li>
    <li>Pass-through charging</li>
    <li>Aircraft-grade aluminum</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Cons:</strong>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>$200 is premium pricing</li>
    <li>Heavy at 1.4 lbs</li>
    <li>100W max (not enough for 16" MacBook Pro at full speed)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Pricing:</strong> $200
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Best for:</strong> Power users who need maximum capacity within airline limits and charge multiple
    devices simultaneously.
  </p>
  <AffiliateButton
      href="/go/amazon/zendure-supertank"
      text="Check Zendure SuperTank Price on Amazon"
      variant="secondary"
      program="amazon"
  />

  <!-- Baseus 65W -->
  <h3 id="baseus-65w">4. Baseus 65W — Best Budget Laptop Charger</h3>
  <p>
    The Baseus 65W proves you don't need to spend $100+ for laptop charging capability. At $50, it offers
